---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const { locale } = Astro.props;

const pageTitle = "Privacy Policy | Luis Ferreira Transfers and Services";
const pageDescription =
  "Learn how Luis Ferreira collects, uses and protects your personal data when you enquire about or book transfers, cleaning services or accommodation.";
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle} pageDescription={pageDescription} bodyClass="secondary-page">
  <section class="cmp-hero-section" aria-labelledby="hero-section">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--tablet-48">
      <div class="hero__text-container">
        <h1 id="hero-section" class="cmp-hero-heading">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>

        <ol class="privacy-list">
          <li>
            <h2>Introduction</h2>
            Luis Ferreira respects your privacy and is committed to protecting your personal data in accordance with the
            General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and applicable Portuguese data protection legislation. This
            Privacy Policy explains what personal information we collect, how we use it, how it is protected and what
            rights you have when using our website or contacting us about our services.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Data Controller</h2>
            The data controller responsible for processing your personal data is Luis Ferreira, based in Portugal. For
            questions about this Privacy Policy or the handling of your personal information, you can contact us at
            lfdsf57@gmail.com or +351 966 831 360.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Personal Information We Collect</h2>
            We collect only the personal information necessary to respond to enquiries and arrange our services. When
            you submit a transfer booking request through our website, we collect your first name, surname, email
            address, telephone number, pickup location and drop-off location. We do not request additional personal
            information through this transfer form unless it is necessary for a particular booking and is communicated
            to you.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Communication Through WhatsApp</h2>
            Customers may contact us directly through WhatsApp to enquire about transfers, cleaning services, the
            advertised rental property or other matters relating to our services. Information shared through WhatsApp
            may include your name, telephone number, messages, booking details and any other personal information you
            choose to provide. These communications are processed to respond to enquiries, coordinate services and
            manage any resulting arrangements. WhatsApp is operated by a third party and its own privacy terms and data
            processing practices also apply to the use of that service.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>How We Use Your Personal Data</h2>
            We use personal information only for relevant business purposes, including responding to enquiries,
            preparing quotations, arranging and managing transfer bookings, coordinating pickup and drop-off details,
            communicating with customers, organising requested cleaning services and responding to enquiries about the
            rental property advertised on our website. We may also process information where necessary to comply with
            legal obligations or establish, exercise or defend legal claims.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
            Personal data is processed where necessary to take steps requested by you before entering into a contract,
            perform a contract, comply with a legal obligation or pursue legitimate interests that do not override your
            rights and freedoms. These legitimate interests may include responding to business enquiries, managing
            communications and maintaining appropriate records of services provided. Where consent is legally required
            for a particular processing activity, we will request it separately.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h3>Sharing of Personal Information</h3>
            We do not sell your personal information to third parties. When you submit a transfer booking request, your
            information is stored in a Google Sheets spreadsheet and used to manage and organise bookings through a
            linked calendar. Where necessary to fulfil your booking, relevant information may be shared with the
            transport provider responsible for the transfer. Personal data may also be processed by Google and other
            relevant service providers operating the systems used to manage bookings and communications, or disclosed to
            public authorities where required by law.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h3>Third-Party Services and Data Processing</h3>
            We use Google services, including Google Sheets and Google and Apple calendar, to store and manage transfer
            booking information. The personal data submitted through the transfer form may therefore be processed by
            Google in accordance with the applicable service terms and privacy documentation. We also use WhatsApp to
            communicate directly with customers who contact us through that service. These third-party providers may
            process personal data in accordance with their own terms, privacy policies and applicable data protection
            obligations. We take reasonable steps to ensure that personal information is handled appropriately when
            using these services.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h3>Data Retention</h3>
            Transfer booking information is retained in our Google Sheets spreadsheet and linked calendar for as long as
            necessary to manage bookings, coordinate services, maintain appropriate business records and comply with
            applicable legal obligations. Information is deleted or anonymised when it is no longer required, unless a
            longer retention period is required or permitted by law. Messages exchanged through WhatsApp may remain
            available in accordance with our own retention practices and the features and settings of that service.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Data Security</h2>
            We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect personal information against
            unauthorised access, accidental loss, disclosure, alteration or destruction. Access to customer information
            is restricted to those who need it for legitimate business purposes. However, no method of electronic
            transmission or storage can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Cookies and Website Technologies</h2>
            Our website may use cookies or similar technologies necessary for its operation. If analytics, advertising
            or other non-essential cookies are implemented, they will be handled in accordance with applicable consent
            and privacy requirements. Information about the cookies actually used by the website and how to manage your
            preferences will be provided through the relevant cookie notice or settings, where applicable.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Your Data Protection Rights</h2>
            Subject to the conditions and exceptions established by applicable law, you may have the right to request
            access to your personal data, correct inaccurate information, request erasure, restrict processing, object
            to certain processing activities and receive data in a portable format where applicable. Where processing is
            based on consent, you may withdraw that consent at any time without affecting the lawfulness of processing
            carried out before withdrawal.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>How to Exercise Your Rights</h2>
            To exercise your data protection rights or ask questions about how your information is used, contact us at
            lfdsf57@gmail.com. We may need to verify your identity before responding to a request. We will handle
            requests within the time limits established by applicable law. Exercising your rights is generally free of
            charge, subject to the exceptions permitted by law.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Right to Lodge a Complaint</h2>
            If you believe that your personal data has been processed unlawfully, you have the right to lodge a
            complaint with the competent supervisory authority. In Portugal, this is the Comissão Nacional de Proteção
            de Dados (CNPD). Further information is available at https://www.cnpd.pt/.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Third-Party Websites and Services</h2>
            Our website may contain links to or provide access to third-party services, including WhatsApp. When you use
            an external service, your information may be processed according to that provider's own privacy policy and
            terms. We are not responsible for the independent privacy practices of third-party services, although our
            own legal obligations remain unaffected.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
            We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes to our services, data processing practices or legal
            requirements. The latest version will be published on this website, together with its effective date. We
            recommend reviewing this policy periodically to remain informed about how personal information is handled.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Contact Information</h2>
            If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or the processing of your personal data, please contact
            Luis Ferreira at lfdsf57@gmail.com or +351 966 831 360.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    margin-left: 1rem;
    list-style: decimal;
    max-width: 60ch;

    h2 {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
